        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-02 15:49:59.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: make target start cheaper",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: make target start cheaper\n\nSetting the debug masks after each target start goes through\nrpc.sh, which costs far more than the three set_param calls it\nruns. Send those as a plain remote command, which is about 2700\nfewer rpc.sh calls across 17 suites. A node reached this way\nalways has Lustre loaded, so rpc.sh's module load is not needed.\n\nThe first mount of a target also sleeps for a second between two\nsyncs to commit the label. sync does not return until the label\nis on disk, so one sync is enough. conf-sanity does this about\n450 times.\n\nMeasured on a single node with pdsh over ssh, the old call took\nabout 0.8 s and the plain remote command about 0.25 s, so roughly\n0.5 s saved per target start. That is about 1350 s across the\n2700 calls of a full pass of the 17 suites. The sync change\nsaves about 1 s each, or about 450 s per conf-sanity run. At\nabout 5900 conf-sanity runs in the last 30 days that is roughly\n2.6 million seconds (about 730 hours) of test time.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id87177ea3c884b55f2ccae9451de6d44cee53de6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
